* explanation command: kubectl delete deployment nginx -n dev-namespace
==> kubectl delete → Deletes a resource
==> deployment nginx → Specifies the Deployment name (nginx)
==> -n dev-namespace → Tells Kubernetes to look inside the namespace dev-namespace

Option 1 — Delete the entire namespace (recommended for cleanup)
This will remove everything inside that namespace (all Deployments, Pods, Services, etc.):
kubectl delete namespace my-namespace

Option 2 — Delete only the Deployment (keep the namespace)
If you only want to remove the Deployment but keep the namespace:
kubectl delete deployment nginx -n my-namespace


